\section{Inferential implementations}{


\strong{Bayesian CAMS} (implemented using bayesmeta/DIRECT). Overall
\code{bmr(m_j ~ pi_j)} and interaction \code{bayesmeta(g_j)}, combined by independent
product quadrature. Posterior inference uses the DIRECT Gaussian-mixture
support, including heterogeneity uncertainty for \(\tau_m\) and
\(\tau_g\). Intervals are \strong{credible intervals}. Reconstruction of CAMS
quantities keeps the required dependence: the joint \((\alpha,\theta)\)
support of the overall block with the independent \(\gamma\) block.
\eqn{\alpha} = overall intercept, \eqn{\theta} = IF slope, \eqn{\gamma} =
interaction mean, stored \code{b_ifrac} is \eqn{\beta = \theta - \gamma}. \verb{$mu}
is the fixed-effect linear predictor. \code{fit$latent$mu_A[[j]]} / \verb{$mu_B[[j]]}
are \strong{trial-specific} \eqn{\mu_{Aj}=m_j-\pi_j g_j},
\eqn{\mu_{Bj}=m_j+(1-\pi_j)g_j}. Population effects at a reporting IF are
\code{\link[=subgroups]{subgroups()}}:
\eqn{\mu_A(\pi)=\alpha+\pi b_{\mathrm{ifrac}}},
\eqn{\mu_B(\pi)=\alpha+\pi b_{\mathrm{ifrac}}+\gamma}.

\strong{Frequentist CAMS} (implemented using metafor). Same factorization and
the same CAMS estimands, with \code{rma} (REML/ML). \verb{$draws} is one
point-estimate row. Intervals are \strong{confidence intervals} from the stored
\code{rma} covariance.

Bayesian CAMS places independent \eqn{N} on \eqn{(\alpha,\theta)} and
\eqn{\gamma} (bmr/bayesmeta).
