\section{Analysis, inference, and implementation}{


These are three separate axes, recorded on \verb{$analysis}, \verb{$inference},
\verb{$engine}, \verb{$method}, \verb{$algorithm}, and \verb{$capabilities}. DA and AD are
not inherently frequentist; CAMS is not inherently Bayesian. IF
functionality (\verb{$capabilities$ifrac}) is \code{TRUE} only for CAMS. See
